{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310819,"nonce":"R03QWpGlLByGr0Qf+7x1AHf8qAM=","title":"2026-06-08 session — runtime-core extraction (Phase 1) + WASM ports of Tensor lifetime, Q4_K_M matmul, flash-attn + softmax + RMSNorm ...","message":"Single-session ladder from \"runtime-wasm has 4 raw-pointer F32 primitives\"\nto \"wasmtime executes the full F32 + Q4_K_M kernel surface a Llama\nforward-pass needs, with parity against scalar references\". Closed Phase 1\n(runtime-core extraction) end-to-end; closed Phases 2-4 of the WASM port.\nWhat remains for actually streaming tokens in a browser tab: KV cache +\nsampling + GGUF loader (Phase 5), threading via Web Workers (Phase 6),\ndeployment with COOP/COEP (Phase 7).\n\nReference plan: [docs/design/wasm_runtime_parity.md](../../../docs/design/wasm_runtime_parity.md).\n\n\n| Phase | Commit | Headline |\n|---|---|---|\n| pre | `d3f1fae` | nue/ARCHITECTURE.md — synthesised module-layer reference |\n| 1 Step 2 | `23bd25e` | tensor_simd.rs (~1050 LOC) → `runtime-core::simd::tensor_f32` |\n| 1 Step 3 | (squashed) | quant types + block ops (Q4_K_M, Q6_K, Q8_K, INT8) → runtime-core |\n| 1 Step 4 | `9a7b51f` | SDOT kernels (c5ab136 + acb80e5 + a241cc9 perf wins) → `runtime-core::quant::sdot` |\n| 1 Step 5 | `86c0220` | dot_f32_simd + Q8K prep helpers → `runtime-core::quant::matmul` |\n| 1 Step 6 | `0d3528d` | recent_contains topk helper → `runtime-core::tensor::topk` |\n| bench | `7ac7a41` | BENCH_RUN_SPACING knob for thermal-cooldown between bench runs |\n| 2 | `f4b7548` | runtime-wasm `Tensor` lifetime + F32 `matmul_t` |\n| 3 | `1e77b83` | runtime-wasm `QTensor` + Q4_K_M loader + `matmul_qt_t_f32` (scalar Q4_K_M dot path extracted to `runtime-core::quant::q4_k_m::vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K_scalar`) |\n| 4a | `3e1ea0a` | `flash_attn_decode_one_qhead` → runtime-core with generic exp parameter; native delegates with `\\|x\\| x.exp()` |\n| 4b | `87156d0` | runtime-wasm FFI exports for flash-attn / softmax / RMSNorm (with `libm::expf`, `libm::sqrtf`) |\n\n`runtime/src/quant.rs` lines: **4 824 → 3 232 (−33%)**.\n`runtime/src/tensor.rs` lines: 4 899 → 4 825 (small set, most of the\nfile is FFI + allocator that stays native).\n\n\n- **runtime-core/** is `#![cfg_attr(not(test), no_std)]` with workspace\n  `lto = \"thin\"`. Hot-path symbols `dot_slice_f32`, `axpy_f16/bf16_slice`\n  and the flash-attn / softmax / RMSNorm kernels are `#[inline(always)]`\n  so cross-crate inlining survives without depending on fat LTO.\n- **Native SDOT** stays gated `#[cfg(all(target_arch = \"aarch64\",\n  target_feature = \"dotprod\"))]` with `#[target_feature(enable = \"dotprod\")]`\n  and the unstable `feature(stdarch_neon_dotprod)` crate attribute.\n  On wasm32 the gate is hard-off and the runtime-core sdot module\n  doesn't even compile in (`#![cfg]` at file level).\n- **`vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K` dispatcher** stays in runtime/src/quant.rs\n  because it reads `RAYZOR_USE_SDOT` (env var). It now routes:\n  SDOT path on aarch64+dotprod with env gate, otherwise\n  `runtime_core::quant::q4_k_m::vec_dot_q4_K_q8_K_scalar`. The wasm\n  build skips the dispatcher and calls the scalar directly.\n- **Generic-over-exp / generic-over-sqrt**:\n  `flash_attn_decode_one_qhead\u003cF: Fn(f32) -\u003e f32\u003e`,\n  `softmax_inplace_f32\u003cF: Fn(f32) -\u003e f32\u003e`,\n  `rms_norm_row_f32\u003cF: Fn(f32) -\u003e f32\u003e` accept the math primitive as\n  a parameter. Native passes `|x| x.exp()` / `f32::sqrt`. WASM passes\n  `libm::expf` / `libm::sqrtf`. Monomorphises per call site;\n  `#[inline(always)]` makes the closure fold into the caller.\n  Earlier `libm::expf` everywhere costed measurable wall on the\n  Llama softmax loop (cache_len × n_q_heads × n_layers × tokens calls\n  per decode) because macOS `f32::exp()` routes through\n  Accelerate-tuned `libsystem_m`. The generic split keeps both paths\n  optimal.\n- **Workspace `lto = \"thin\"`** introduced in commit `23bd25e`. The\n  per-crate `[profile.release]` blocks in runtime/Cargo.toml and\n  runtime-core/Cargo.toml were silently ignored by cargo; only the\n  workspace root profile takes effect. Build time +20%.\n\n\n`runtime-wasm/Cargo.toml` depends on `rayzor-runtime-core`.\n`runtime-wasm/.cargo/config.toml` runs cargo test through\n`wasmtime -S threads -W threads -W shared-memory` so the WASM unit\ntests execute directly. 6/6 tests pass:\n\n```\ntest tensor::tests::zeros_then_get_flat_returns_zero                  ok\ntest tensor::tests::matmul_t_64x64_matches_reference                  ok\ntest qtensor::tests::matmul_qt_t_q4_k_m_matches_dequant_reference     ok\ntest kernels::tests::softmax_inplace_normalises_and_sums_to_one       ok\ntest kernels::tests::rms_norm_matches_scalar_reference                ok\ntest kernels::tests::flash_attn_decode_matches_reference_single_head  ok\n```\n\nArtefact size: **85 KB** for the full Phase 1-4 surface (was 76 KB\npre-extraction).\n\nFFI exports the WASM crate now ships (Haxe-callable via the same\n`rayzor_*` symbol convention as native):\n\n| Group | Symbols |\n|---|---|\n| Tensor lifetime | `rayzor_tensor_zeros`, `_full`, `_from_floats`, `_ndim`, `_numel`, `_dtype`, `_data`, `_shape_ptr`, `_get_flat_f32`, `_free` |\n| QTensor / Q4_K_M | `rayzor_qtensor_from_bytes_q4_k_m`, `_rows`, `_cols`, `_scheme`, `_free` |\n| Matmul | `rayzor_tensor_matmul_t`, `rayzor_tensor_matmul_qt_t_f32` |\n| Transformer | `rayzor_tensor_flash_attn_decode_f32`, `_softmax_inplace_f32`, `_rms_norm_f32` |\n| Pre-Phase-1 (legacy) | `rayzor_tensor_simd_add_f32`, `_mul_f32`, `_dot_f32`, `_axpy_f32`, `_sum_f32` (kept for compat) |\n\n\nCool-state bench, M1 Pro, Llama 3.2 1B Q4_K_M, N=600 Paris-history\nprompt, 5 runs spaced 90s, `BENCH_RUN_SPACING=90`:\n\n- Step 6 baseline (pre-Phase-4): median 63.34 tok/s (range 62.5–64.6, σ=0.91)\n- Phase 4a (flash-attn delegated): median 63.91 tok/s (range 57.9–65.8, σ=3.35)\n\nWithin noise. Wider stddev is post-LLVM-build thermal recovery on\nruns 1-2; runs 3-5 hit 63.9 / 65.6 / 65.8 — steady-state parity.\n\nCritical: `#[inline(always)]` on the runtime-core kernels is\nload-bearing. Without it thin-LTO occasionally declined to inline\nthe closure-bearing generic and the softmax loop took a ~3% hit\n(measured on Phase 4a first bench: median 56.6, range 52.3–64.4).\n\n`cargo test -p rayzor-runtime --lib`: 105/105 pass throughout.\n`cargo test -p rayzor-runtime-core --lib`: 12/12 pass.\n\n\nThe plan numbers from\n[wasm_runtime_parity.md](../../../docs/design/wasm_runtime_parity.md):\n\n- **Phase 5** — KV cache + sampling + GGUF loader (1-2 weeks)\n  - KV cache: pure-Haxe wrapper in `nue/transformer/KVCache.hx`\n    already exists; needs WASM Tensor allocation only. Should be\n    trivial once Phase 4 kernels land.\n  - Sampling: argmax / top-k / top-p. Pure scalar, small.\n  - GGUF loader: the long pole (~500 LOC parser). Browser side\n    needs `fetch()` + ArrayBuffer; wasmtime side uses\n    `std::fs::read`. Probably benefits from an abstract byte-source\n    trait.\n- **Phase 6** — threading (2-3 weeks)\n  - `wasm32-wasip1-threads` for the wasmtime / CLI path (worker\n    pool abstracts over `std::thread::spawn`, picks up the WASI\n    impl automatically).\n  - Browser path: `runtime-wasm/wasm32_browser_workers.rs` wraps\n    Web Worker spawn via JS imports (`spawn_worker`, `notify`,\n    `wait`).\n  - Single-threaded fallback for COOP/COEP-disabled deployments.\n- **Phase 7** — browser deployment (1 week)\n  - Dev server with COOP/COEP headers (`tools/wasm-dev-serve/`).\n  - `coi-serviceworker` integration for GitHub Pages-style hosts.\n  - `examples/wasm-features/llama-chat/` browser demo.\n\n\n- **Thermal sensitivity is real.** Cool-state benches need at least\n  60-90s between runs after any LLVM build. `BENCH_RUN_SPACING`\n  env var in `tools/llama-diff/bench.sh` controls it. First 1-2\n  runs after a fresh build always read low because the M1 Pro\n  package is still cooling from the LLVM compile.\n- **WASM build requires nightly.** `runtime-core` has\n  `#![cfg_attr(target_arch = \"aarch64\", feature(stdarch_neon_dotprod))]`.\n  The wasm32 build cfg-skips it but nightly is needed to PARSE the\n  attribute. `runtime-wasm/build.sh` uses `cargo +nightly`.\n- **`runtime-wasm` is excluded from the workspace.** Top-level\n  `Cargo.toml` excludes it; it has its own `.cargo/config.toml`\n  with wasm32-specific rustflags (+atomics, +bulk-memory,\n  +mutable-globals, +simd128, +relaxed-simd, link-arg\n  --shared-memory, --import-memory, --max-memory=1 GiB).\n- **The `f16` import in runtime/src/quant.rs is `#[cfg(test)]`-gated\n  now.** The non-test code path no longer references it directly\n  (all f16 use moved to runtime-core types). Don't reintroduce as\n  unconditional `use half::f16;` — clippy will fail under\n  `-D warnings`.\n\n\n- [[perf_spin_wait_worker_pool]] — the prior session's 4001079\n  perf win. Still in `runtime/src/worker_pool.rs`; doesn't move to\n  runtime-core because it depends on `std::thread`.\n- [[perf_q4km_llamacpp_kernel_port]] — c5ab136 SDOT win. Now lives\n  in `runtime-core::quant::sdot::dot_q4_k_q8_kblock_llamacpp`.\n- [[perf_flash_attn_decode]] — 7835a26 fused-attn win. The inner\n  per-q_head kernel now lives in\n  `runtime-core::tensor::flash_attn::flash_attn_decode_one_qhead`.\n- [[project_wasm_phase2]] — outdated as of this arc. The \"TensorDemo\n  arity mismatch\" framing was true in May 2026 but is irrelevant\n  now: wasm32 tests run cleanly under wasmtime with the runner\n  config in runtime-wasm/.cargo/config.toml.\n- [[project_wasm_roadmap]] / [[project_wasm_status]] — older WASM\n  status docs. Update or supersede when Phase 5 lands.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_wasm_parity_arc` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}